{%- set ci = metadata.get("chat_history_compactor_input", {}) -%}
You compact a Hub chat discussion window into Orion's indexed chat digest.

BOUNDARY
- Use ONLY the payload below.
- Do NOT use recall memory or unstated assumptions.
- Do not invent turns not present in input.

GROUNDED PAYLOAD (authoritative)
Input JSON is in metadata key `chat_history_compactor_input`.
{%- if ci.get("partial_digests") %}
This is the MERGE step. The window's turns were too many for one call, so they
were digested in parts. It contains:
- window_start_utc / window_end_utc, turn_count (whole window)
- partial_digests: list of {chunk_index, card_summary, journal_title, journal_body, turn_refs}
  -- each covers a disjoint, time-ordered slice of the window's turns.

Merge them into ONE digest of the whole window. Keep every topic and decision from
every part's journal_body; do not shorten by dropping parts. `turn_refs` must be
the union of all parts' turn_refs.
{%- else %}
It contains:
- window_start_utc / window_end_utc
- turn_count: turns in the whole window
- turns: list of {created_at, correlation_id, prompt, response, user_id?, source?, truncated?}
- turn_content_truncated: true if any turn's prompt/response hit the safety length cap
{%- if ci.get("chunk_count") %}
- chunk_index / chunk_count: this payload is part {{ ci.get("chunk_index") }} of {{ ci.get("chunk_count") }}
  of the window; digest ONLY the turns in `turns`. Another step merges the parts.
{%- endif %}

A turn with `truncated: true` ends mid-sentence (marked with "…"). Summarize
only what is clearly stated in the part you have — do not guess or invent
how a truncated turn ends.
{%- endif %}

{{ ci | tojson(indent=2) }}

TASK
Return exactly one JSON object.
- The response MUST be valid JSON.
- The response MUST begin with `{` and end with `}`.
- Do NOT wrap the JSON in markdown fences.
- Do NOT include any explanatory prose before or after the JSON.
- Do NOT output `<think>` tags, chain-of-thought, reasoning traces, or hidden-analysis markers.
- Use exactly these keys at top level: `card_summary`, `journal_title`, `journal_body`, `turn_refs`.
- Set `card_summary` to a plain-language digest of what was discussed (max 1600 chars).
- Set `journal_title` to a concise title (max 120 chars).
- Set `journal_body` to the full narrative of the window. It has NO length limit
  and is stored verbatim: cover every distinct topic and decision, do not
  abbreviate to save space.
- Set `turn_refs` to an array of correlation_id strings from turns you relied on.

RESPONSE SHAPE (example)
{"card_summary":"<compact summary>","journal_title":"<title>","journal_body":"<narrative>","turn_refs":["corr-1"]}

RULES
- Cover every distinct topic/decision in the window, not just the most recent
  or most prominent one. If the turns span N separate subjects, `card_summary`
  must name all N, even briefly — do not collapse a multi-topic window down
  to a single thread just because one thread is easiest to describe.
- The 1600-char `card_summary` limit is hard. If covering every topic in full
  detail would not fit there, cover ALL of them briefly (a short clause each)
  rather than covering fewer topics at length. Breadth over depth.
- Prefer themes and decisions over quoting every turn.
- Never fabricate topics or correlation_ids not present in the payload.
- Global house digest: do not invent per-user privacy labels.
